   "text": "[Heading: High Voltage Inverter Fault]\nThe Panasonic H98 error code specifically points to a High Voltage (HV) Inverter power fault, which typically means the inverter board is failing to supply the correct voltage to the magnetron or there is a fault within the high-voltage circuit itself. Because this involves internal components that store lethal voltages even when unplugged, you cannot safely fix this yourself. Please stop using the appliance immediately and contact Panasonic support or a qualified microwave repair engineer for diagnosis and part replacement."
